WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.730
Speaker 1: A geopolitical story of consequence
that developed over the last 24 hours, which

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:09.400
is really just as much about reporting as
it is about foreign policy.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:17.420
There were initial reports yesterday that
missiles had struck Poland, and the initial

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:24.900
belief was this was Russia probably accidentally
in targeting Ukraine.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.490
Although it was not completely clear.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:34.899
And the belief now is that this was actually
an accident committed by Ukrainian forces.

00:00:34.899 --> 00:00:39.550
The latest reporting from CNN as of this morning.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:47.090
Poland's president says missile that killed
two likely fired by Ukraine in defense against

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:49.210
a Russian attack.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.300
Polish president said the missile.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.629
Polish President Duda said the missile that
killed two people in eastern Poland Tuesday

00:00:55.629 --> 00:01:00.949
was likely fired by Ukrainian forces, defending
against a wave of Russian missile strikes

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:03.399
and that the incident appeared to be an accident.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:08.180
Quote, There is no indication that this was
an intentional attack on Poland.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:13.000
Most likely it was a Russian made S-300 rocket
that was in a tweet.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.320
He later told a press conference there's a
high chance it was an air defense missile

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.240
from the Ukrainian side, which fell on Polish
territory in an accident while intercepting

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.140
incoming Russian missiles.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.360
Duda's comments were in line with those of
two officials briefed on initial U.S. assessments

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:35.470
who told CNN it appears the missile originated
in Ukraine, although it was Russian made.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:39.740
This is important because listen, there's
so many stories here.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.950
Number one.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.360
These military actions are serious business.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:51.350
And when we talk about innocent bystanders,
you're no more innocent.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:56.770
If you're in Poland where two were killed
than you are in Ukraine, where the exact same

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:57.770
thing would happen.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:02.810
Either way, when we're talking about innocent
bystanders, we're talking about innocent bystanders.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:08.420
But the unintended consequences of.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:15.470
An invasion of Ukraine by Russia are extraordinarily
far reaching in ways that aren't even always

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:20.770
considered sort of as the primary question
or discussion.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:26.959
The second thing that's important to mention
is the amount of misinformation and disinformation

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:33.269
and conspiracy theories that floated around
in the roughly 8 to 10 hours after the original

00:02:33.269 --> 00:02:34.790
reporting was.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.860
This seems to have been Russia.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.610
Russia bombed Poland.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:39.610
Okay.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.060
We saw all of the following and more.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:49.300
We saw Fox News personalities say Poland should
bomb Russia in response.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.700
You can't let Russia get away with this.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.000
Well, it turns out it wasn't Russia.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:59.050
Now, can you blame Russia because Ukraine
is defending itself from Russian aggression?

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.050
Well, okay, you can have that conversation.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:06.680
But these hawks on right wing media saying
anything short of immediately bombing Russia

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.060
back is unacceptable.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.940
It's weak, it's sexy, whatever the case may
be.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.021
Russia didn't actually do this.

00:03:12.021 --> 00:03:14.150
This was an accident from Ukraine.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.280
Based on what we know right now, that's number
one.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.440
Number two, conspiracy theories.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:18.640
I'm not even going to play it.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.090
I was going to play it.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.190
And they said, why even bother?

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.190
Conspiracy theory.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.640
Charlie Kirk saying, I don't know.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.150
I hope this isn't a false flag.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.310
I hope this isn't a false flag.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.200
I have no evidence that it's a false flag,
but I just hope it isn't.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:39.660
And one of the things that unfortunately happens
in the 24 hour news cycle and again, this

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.860
is why sometimes I can't do it because the
story is so big.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:48.340
But in the 24 hour news cycle, particularly
when there are shootings and crimes, I will

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:56.180
often wait an extra day to avoid fueling disinformation
or conspiracy theories.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:00.210
And sometimes you just have to wait a little
bit, particularly when the news is coming

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.420
from half a world away.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:06.579
Not that there isn't internet and reporting
in those places, but we don't always figure

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.060
out exactly what's going on right away.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:15.580
So this is now another dimension to what's
going on in the Russian invasion of Ukraine.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.150
This has been going on now for months and
months.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.150
We don't know how long it's going to go.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.470
We still don't know what Putin's end game
is.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.490
We still don't know what the ultimate resolution
is.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.990
There are now divided.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:30.110
There have always been that there are increasingly
divided opinions about for how long and to

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:37.650
what degree should or should the United States
not be funding Ukraine's defense, be it through

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.919
money or be it through weaponry and equipment?

00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:45.981
And we are now in a nine month conflict, it's
shocking to say, but it was I believe it was

00:04:45.981 --> 00:04:48.380
February when we first started reporting on
this.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.470
We're now almost in December.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:53.070
I have no idea what the conclusion of this
is going to be.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:58.190
But what we do know is the longer it goes
on just simply from a sort of like entropy

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:05.389
and statistical perspective, the more likely
it is that more types of innocent bystanders

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:07.780
are going to be hurt and are going to be killed.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:14.940
Good use of restraint, by the way, by many
in the United States, not Fox News, not Charlie

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.789
Kirk, but by many of the United States in
actually waiting until we have more information

00:05:18.789 --> 00:05:20.700
about exactly what it is that happened there.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:25.650
And it now appears that it was actually an
errant Ukrainian defense attempt that ended

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:27.470
up killing two people in Poland.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:30.000
What should the geopolitical consequences
of that be?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.000
I don't know.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:06:25.710
And we don't yet know what the parties involved

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:38.160
are thinking.

